Graphviz (14.1.2 and 16.1.0 alike): a label whose first line is empty ("\n\nTitle") leaves the first text span
half-initialised. storeline() takes the span array from gv_recalloc(NULL, 1, 2, …), which zeroes only the bytes
beyond the "old" first element; for an empty line neither textspan_size() nor anything else then sets span->layout
and span->free_layout, and free_textspan() later calls free_layout through whatever the memory held. Natively the
memory is usually zero and nothing happens (valgrind: "Conditional jump or move depends on uninitialised value(s)
at free_textspan (labels.c:197)"); in WebAssembly the call traps ("table index is out of bounds"), so valid graphs —
records with rankdir, the "crazy" example — could not be drawn. Found in the Nov 2026 bug hunt; worth reporting
upstream (gitlab.com/graphviz/graphviz).
--- a/lib/common/labels.c
+++ b/lib/common/labels.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
     lp->u.txt.span = gv_recalloc(lp->u.txt.span, oldsz, oldsz + 1,
                                  sizeof(textspan_t));
     span = &lp->u.txt.span[lp->u.txt.nspans];
+    *span = (textspan_t){0};
     span->str = line;
     span->just = terminator;
     if (line && line[0]) {
